```
.grid3{align-items:stretch}
.qcard{display:flex;flex-direction:column}
.rank-list{...}
.qcard__foot{margin-top:auto}
```
Then all cards in a row equal height (grid stretch default), and the foot sits at bottom. The lists have different content heights; `margin-top:auto` on foot pushes it down. That handles wrapping gracefully. But if one card is taller, all get taller; fine. Currently `align-items:start`; change to `stretch`. For single-column, no difference. Add `display:flex;flex-direction:column` to `.qcard`, and `.qcard__foot{margin-top:auto}`. The list isn't flex-grow; the foot pushes to bottom. This yields a consistent look. At 901, cards all 323 high, footers aligned. Nice. But does `.qcard` as flex affect list margin collapse? No. The list width auto fills. Good.

Let's implement.

